(## 5. Retrieval Code Walkthrough) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `Pseudonymizer`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`Pseudonymizer` receives `FHIR_PSEUDONYMIZATION_KEY` from the environment.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`identifier\(resource_type, raw_id\)` computes an HMAC-SHA256 digest over the resource) Tj
0 -12 Td
(type and source ID, then prefixes a shortened digest with `PAT`, `OBS`, `ENC`, or) Tj
0 -12 Td
(another resource prefix. The HMAC prevents someone with only the output database from) Tj
0 -12 Td
(reversing the pseudonym.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`patient_offset\(patient_id\)` derives a stable integer from the same key, in the range) Tj
0 -12 Td
(-365 to +365 days. `shift_date\(value, offset_days\)` parses an ISO date or timestamp and) Tj
0 -12 Td
(applies that offset. If shifting would move a date outside the valid calendar range \(an) Tj
0 -12 Td
(edge case seen with a small number of public HAPI test records near year 1 or year) Tj
0 -12 Td
(9999\), the original value is kept unshifted instead of raising an error, so one unusual) Tj
0 -12 Td
(record cannot crash an entire retrieval.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
ET
endstream
