(### `FHIRRetriever.__init__`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(The constructor validates retry, page-size, and limit settings, opens the local) Tj
0 -12 Td
(cache/checkpoint paths, configures the HTTP session, opens SQLite, and hydrates the) Tj
0 -12 Td
(database from the full local cache. No network request happens during construction.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `_make_session`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(This method creates a `requests.Session` with an `HTTPAdapter` and `urllib3.Retry`) Tj
0 -12 Td
(policy. It retries only GET requests for transient status codes such as 429 and 503,) Tj
0 -12 Td
(uses exponential backoff, honors `Retry-After`, and supplies a descriptive User-Agent.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `_fetch_pages`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(FHIR search results are Bundles. This loop requests one Bundle page, validates the) Tj
0 -12 Td
(response, persists its resources, reads the Bundle `next` link, and repeats until there) Tj
0 -12 Td
(is no next page or an optional resource limit is reached. A request error, invalid JSON,) Tj
0 -12 Td
(or invalid Bundle becomes a `RetrievalFailure`; the partial resources already persisted) Tj
0 -12 Td
(remain available.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `_pseudonymize_resource`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(This method runs before data is persisted. It copies a FHIR resource, replaces resource) Tj
0 -12 Td
(IDs and references with stable pseudonyms, shifts relevant dates, and removes Patient) Tj
0 -12 Td
(identifiers, telecom details, addresses, contacts, and communication preferences.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Patient family and given names are extracted from the FHIR `name` field into internal) Tj
0 -12 Td
(fields before the original `name` array is removed, so they can still be stored in the) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`patients` table. Observation and Encounter references are rewritten so relationships) Tj
0 -12 Td
(survive.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `_sync_single_patient_scope`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(Called whenever a command targets one specific Patient \(`--patient-id`, `--patient-) Tj
0 -12 Td
(observations-encounters`, and the underlying `get_patient`/`get_*_for_patient`) Tj
0 -12 Td
(functions\). It removes rows for any other Patient from the `patients`, `conditions`,) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`observations`, and `encounters` tables, then re-syncs only that Patient's cached data.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(This keeps single-Patient commands scoped to the requested Patient, even when the same) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`--output-dir` was previously used for `--all-patients` or a different Patient.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `_load_related`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(This method loops over the requested Patients and resource types. It performs a separate) Tj
0 -12 Td
(FHIR search for each combination, for example `Observation?patient=<source-id>`. The) Tj
0 -12 Td
(checkpoint uses pseudonymized query identifiers, while source IDs only remain in process) Tj
0 -12 Td
(memory long enough to perform requests.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `FHIRDatabase.sync`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(`sync` receives de-identified resources and performs SQLite inserts/upserts. Stable) Tj
0 -12 Td
(primary keys for Patients, Conditions, Observations, and Encounters mean a later run) Tj
0 -12 Td
(updates rows instead of adding duplicates, so loads are idempotent.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(### `export_csv`) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
(After a retrieval operation, SQLite tables are exported to CSV, overwriting any existing) Tj
0 -12 Td
(files. Headers are read from `PRAGMA table_info`, so CSV column order follows the active) Tj
0 -12 Td
(SQLite schema. Export happens after every database sync during a run, not only once at) Tj
0 -12 Td
(the end.) Tj
0 -12 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
